<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  NexusCheatFramework — Cheat Manager Shortcut Toolbox Entry

  This XML inserts an entry into etaHEN's Toolbox that opens the
  NexusCheatFramework cheat manager overlay in the PS4/PS5 browser
  with autoOpen=1, so the cheat manager view appears immediately.

  Place this file in:
    /data/etaHEN/toolbox/

  The file must be named with a .xml extension (e.g. cheat_manager.xml).

  IMPORTANT: EDIT THIS FILE BEFORE USE
  - Replace <host-pc-ip> with your HOST PC's actual IP address (not the console IP).
  - Replace <port> with your WebUI listen port (default 9080).
  - Example: http://192.168.1.100:9080/?autoOpen=1

  PREREQUISITES:
  1. NexusFramework payload loaded on the PS4/PS5 (via etaHEN, GoldHEN, etc.)
  2. NCF WebUI running on a PC on the same network:
       dotnet run --project src/NexusCheatFramework.Web -- --ip <console-ip> --port 9080
  3. This file placed in /data/etaHEN/toolbox/ on the console

  HOW IT WORKS:
  - Clicking this entry opens the PS4/PS5 browser to the NCF WebUI.
  - The ?autoOpen=1 query parameter tells the WebUI to immediately show
    the cheat manager overlay (no need to press the keyboard shortcut).
  - From the overlay you can browse cheats, toggle them on/off, and
    close the overlay to return to the game.

  This is NOT a native cheat engine. It is a browser-based remote control flow.
  See docs/CHEAT_MANAGER_SHORTCUT.md for full walkthrough.

  Attribution: Derived from etaHEN toolbox XML format patterns.
  See https://github.com/etaHEN/etaHEN for the official format.
-->
<toolbox version="1.0">
  <category name="Homebrew">
    <item name="NCF Cheat Manager">
      <!--
        IMPORTANT: Replace <host-pc-ip> and <port> below with your actual values.
        Example: http://192.168.1.100:9080/?autoOpen=1
      -->
      <action type="open_uri">http://<host-pc-ip>:<port>/?autoOpen=1</action>
      <description>
        Opens the NexusCheatFramework cheat manager overlay in the browser.
        The overlay appears immediately (autoOpen mode).
        Prerequisites:
        1. NexusFramework payload loaded on this console
        2. NCF WebUI running on a PC on the same network:
           dotnet run --project src/NexusCheatFramework.Web -- --ip &lt;console-ip&gt; --port 9080
        3. Edit this XML file to replace &lt;host-pc-ip&gt; and &lt;port&gt; with your PC's IP and port
      </description>
    </item>
  </category>
</toolbox>
